.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1036 AM PDT Fri Oct 9 2026

Strong onshore flow aloft is aiding in the retention of the LIFR-
MVFR stratus deck across the region with clearing times generally
later than the previous forecast. Still expecting inland terminals
to generally clear around 18-20Z while the coastal region remains
socked in through the day. Strong onshore winds will develop through
the day with gusts up to 20 knots, with some diminishing possible
overnight as the lower layers decouple. Some LLWS concerns are
present in the interior overnight, particularly at LVK, but they are
not strong enough to mention in the TAFs. Opted to keep the
generally persistent forecast for stratus formation tonight owing to
uncertainty surrounding an approaching cold front, which may allow
stratus to dissipate or ceilings to lift. Beyond the 24-hour TAF
period, expect stronger winds to develop through Saturday.

Vicinity of SFO... VFR at the terminal through the day with a low to
moderate confidence for ceilings around 11-15Z Saturday morning,
held off on issuing a BKN line. Strong west winds will develop
through the afternoon and evening hours, with low to moderate
confidence in the wind speeds overnight as the surface winds
decouple. Strong southwest winds are possible late this evening into
the overnight hours, with the winds continuing to strengthen as they
veer to the west-northwest Saturday afternoon. Gusts above 35 kt are
not expected today or Saturday, but may need to see how the winds
develop today.

SFO Bridge Approach... Stratus remains in the corridor north of SJC
and south of the San Mateo Bridge, with moderate confidence of
dissipation around 18-19Z. Otherwise similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals... IFR stratus is expected to linger through
the day at MRY with a brief scattering in the afternoon at best, and
may clear out at SNS within the next couple of hours. Stratus is
expected to return this evening with LIFR conditions possible
overnight. A moderate onshore breeze is expected this afternoon and
late Saturday morning, persisting after the end of the TAF period.
Any influences from the incoming cold front will come after the TAF
period ends.

