.MARINE...
(Today through Wednesday)
Issued at 1036 AM PDT Fri Oct 9 2026

Strong northerly breezes will continue to spread into the
northern waters today with frequent gale force gusts expected by
tonight. Widespread hazardous conditions are expected by Saturday
morning through at least Sunday morning as strong to near gale
northwesterly breezes spread across the waters and build rough to
very rough seas. Long period southerly swell arriving today will
collide with long period northwesterly swell Sunday, creating a
confused sea state. Conditions will improve by Monday night as
northerly breezes diminish to become gentle to moderate and seas
subside to become moderate.

