.BEACHES...
Issued at 446 AM PDT Fri Oct 9 2026

Hazardous beach conditions will be present at Pacific Coast beaches
Saturday through Monday. Long period southerly swell from distant
Tropical Storm Rachel will build in height through the weekend,
bringing an increased risk of sneaker waves and strong rip currents.
Long period westerly swell from a gale force low in the Central
North Pacific will arrive Sunday, bringing breaking waves up to 16
feet. The large tidal swings will also result in coastal erosion as
water and waves are brought farther up the beach than normal,
especially during high tide. Remain off jetties, piers, rocks, and
other waterside infrastructure as waves can sweep across the
shoreline without warning, pulling people into the sea. Remain out
of the water to avoid hazardous surf and strong rip currents and
never turn your back on the ocean!

